being a part of the opposite of that  negative common theme is your one word  to gain extra clarity you can combine  multiple words into one word that  carries extra meaning for you  think about if you've always loved this  one word and always will what values you  may have learned from your parents and  is this who you really are as opposed to  someone you think you should be number  four you must overcome your limiting  beliefs you are where you are because of  what you believe and the limit beliefs  that you own have held you back from  doing big things before and will hold  you back again this time around as well  you tell yourself that having one word  is too bold you'll seek out the opinions  of others instead of listening to  yourself more do you worry that someone  else is using that already and you'll  think it's too simple and can't be put  into a single word stop needlessly  overcomplicating things stopped playing  small stop being ruled by the judgements  and opinions of other people it's time  to finally do something big with your  life embrace it number five apply your  one word to your marketing the easiest  way to get started is to build a  marketing campaign around your one word  if your one word is action for example  what's a credo that defines action for  you and your soon to be emerging  movement what's your action founding  story what will you name your action  tribe what rituals and gestures  represent action what's the name of your  company your logo your font and your  symbols and how do they show action what  or who is the enemy of action and how  can you rally against them what does  action sound like your one word sits as  a layer on top of all the important  decisions that you make and your market  is usually the easiest place to start  because it brings in revenue prove to  yourself that it works in small  increments before you go all-in number  six leverage your one word to build an  empire Mickey more sales is great but  your one word has so much greater  potential for your business it can help  you build an empire the next easiest  place to start is your company culture  let's see there one word is care  applying that to your culture how do you  hire with care how do you onboard new  hires with care how do you create an  environment that screens care what  company rituals will you create that  embodied care what titles names in  language will you use around care what  do care company policies look like how  do you fire with care then you can move  to operations thinking about your client  management  buyer selection products and services  quality control research and development  mentors and advisors raising capital  project management and so on how do you  approach each one through the lens of  care what started off as a personal  journey of self-discovery has become a  galvanizing force that can reshape the  way you do business impact every level  of your company and give the people  around you as well as yourself a cause  to believe in find your one word
 

